__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Generated datasets and run outputs — regenerate from configs, never commit.
#
# These are anchored with a leading slash, and must stay that way. An unanchored
# `data/` matches a directory named `data` at *any* depth, which is how the whole
# of `iqssl/data/` was silently excluded from four commits: the package was never
# committed, the session that wrote it ended, and the code was gone. Anchoring
# scopes each rule to the repository root, where the generated artefacts actually
# live. tests/test_scaffold.py::test_every_package_module_is_tracked fails if a
# package module ever goes untracked again.
/data/
/outputs*/
/multirun/
# `/results/*`, not `/results/`, and the difference is the whole point: git
# never descends into an excluded *directory*, so a negation underneath one can
# never fire. `!/results/frozen/` sat below `/results/` for the project's whole
# life and did nothing -- `git check-ignore results/frozen/x.json` reported it
# ignored, and every measured result stayed out of the repository. Excluding the
# directory's *contents* leaves the directory itself walkable, so the negation
# below takes effect. tests/test_scaffold.py::test_frozen_results_are_committable
# fails if this reverts.
/results/*
!/results/frozen/
/wandb/
# Written into the working directory by the Optuna sweeper at the end of a
# sweep, because pretrain.yaml sets hydra.sweep.dir=".". It records only the
# winner, which the run directories already carry in full -- and committing it
# would put one method's tuning result in the repository root as if it were a
# project-level fact. Same family as the `pretrain.log` that got committed
# before `hydra/job_logging: none` was set.
/optimization_results.yaml
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.log
*.npy
*.parquet
# `**/` and not `*/`: a gitignore `*` never crosses a `/`, so the original
# `!/results/frozen/*.parquet` re-included only direct children of frozen/ and
# left `frozen/comparison/headline.parquet` -- where the aggregator actually
# writes -- ignored. `**/` matches zero or more directories, so both depths work.
!/results/frozen/**/*.parquet

.DS_Store
